{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "series-title",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -340,
      "width": 2180,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "# 无穷级数与幂级数\n\n[[01_Math/01_calculus/05_无穷级数与幂级数|从这里连续阅读]] · [[01_Math/01_calculus/05_Infinite_Series_and_Improper_Integrals#Part B：Taylor Series|课堂记录与完整练习]]\n\n从上往下：部分和 → 判别与误差 → 符号与顺序 → 幂级数范围 → Taylor 表示 → 函数计算。卡片打开共享原子；颜色区分论证角色，不表示掌握程度。"
    },
    {
      "id": "g-foundation",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 2180,
      "height": 740,
      "label": "1 · 部分和：什么叫有一个有限的和",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "s001",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 100,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 290,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[无穷级数|Infinite series]]\nFor defined finite real terms, form $S_N=\\sum_{n=1}^N a_n$. The series converges when these partial sums approach a finite number. The term sequence $a_n$ and the total sequence $S_N$ are different; bounded totals alone need not converge.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n各项为已定义的有限实数；先求前 $N$ 项的部分和 $S_N$，再看它是否趋于有限数。通项与累计量是两个数列；部分和仅有界也可能振荡发散。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "s002",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 590,
      "y": 100,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 290,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[级数通项判别|The nth-term divergence test]]\nConvergence of a real series forces $a_n\\to0$. Proving that the terms do not tend to zero proves divergence; a zero term limit is inconclusive. Harmonic terms tend to zero while their partial sums grow without bound.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n实数级数收敛必有 $a_n\\to0$；已证明通项不趋零即可判发散，趋零时仍无结论。调和级数的通项趋零，部分和却无界增长。",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "harmonic",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 100,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 270,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[调和数对数增长|Harmonic growth]]\n\nFor $n\\ge1$, the partial sums satisfy $\\ln(n+1)\\le H_n\\le1+\\ln n$. Terms vanish while totals diverge.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\nn≥1时适用上述界；通项趋零不能保证部分和收敛；调和数按对数尺度无界增长。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s004",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1690,
      "y": 100,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 330,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[望远镜级数|Telescoping series]]\nCancel only inside finite partial sums, retaining all boundary terms. For finite real $b_n$, a fixed positive integer $m$, and an integer $N\\ge m$,\n$$\\sum_{n=m}^{N}(b_n-b_{n+1})=b_m-b_{N+1}.$$\nThis series converges exactly when $b_{N+1}$ has a finite limit. Other cancellation patterns may leave several terms at each end.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n先在有限部分和内消项，保留两端完整表达式。上式中 $m$ 为固定正整数、$N\\ge m$；相邻差形式恰在末端 $b_{N+1}$ 有有限极限时收敛。其他错位形式可能每端留下多项。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "finite-geometric",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 440,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 270,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[几何和|Finite geometric sum]]\n\nCompute a finite partial sum first; ratio 1 is handled by counting terms, with no convergence test needed.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n先算有限项总量；公比1直接数项数，有限求和无需收敛条件。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "s003",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 590,
      "y": 440,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 270,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[几何级数|Geometric series]]\n\nWith a nonzero first term, the partial sums converge exactly when $|r|<1$. The all-zero series converges for every ratio.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n收敛是部分和有有限极限；恒零级数需要单独处理。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "g-tests",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 820,
      "width": 2180,
      "height": 780,
      "label": "2 · 正项与绝对值：找能控制整段尾部的结构",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s010",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 920,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[级数直接比较判别|Direct comparison for series]]\nFor defined finite terms, suppose $0\\le a_n\\le b_n$ eventually. Convergence of $\\sum b_n$ implies convergence of $\\sum a_n$; divergence of $\\sum a_n$ implies divergence of $\\sum b_n$. The reversed comparisons alone are inconclusive.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n各项须有定义且有限，尾部满足 $0\\le a_n\\le b_n$。收敛上界证明收敛，发散下界证明发散；反向比较本身不能判定。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s011",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 590,
      "y": 920,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[级数极限比较判别|Limit comparison for series]]\nFor eventually positive terms, $a_n/b_n\\to L$ with $0<L<\\infty$ gives the same convergence behaviour, not the same sum. Limits $0$ and $+\\infty$ retain only the applicable one-way comparison; failure of the ratio to converge does not prove divergence.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n尾部为正且 $a_n/b_n\\to L$、$0<L<\\infty$ 时同敛散，不表示和相等。比值趋零或正无穷只保留相应单向比较；比值无极限本身也不证明发散。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s012",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 920,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[级数积分判别|The integral test]]\nFor a positive integer $N_0$, let $a_n=f(n)$ on the tail. If $f$ is continuous, positive and nonincreasing on $[N_0,\\infty)$, the series tail and its improper integral converge or diverge together. Their finite values need not be equal.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n正整数 $N_0$ 起，令 $a_n=f(n)$；若 $f$ 在整个 $[N_0,\\infty)$ 上连续、为正且单调不增，级数尾部与对应反常积分同敛散，有限数值不必相等。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s013",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1690,
      "y": 920,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[p级数判别|The p-series test]]\nFor fixed real $p$, $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}n^{-p}$ converges exactly when $p>1$. For $p>0$, use the [[无穷远 p 积分判别|power-tail integral]]; for $p\\le0$, the terms already fail to vanish. At $p=1$ the series diverges despite vanishing terms.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n固定实数 $p$，$\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}n^{-p}$ 恰在 $p>1$ 收敛。正 $p$ 用幂函数尾积分；$p\\le0$ 的项已不趋零。$p=1$ 虽通项趋零仍发散。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s014",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 1260,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[级数比值判别|The ratio test]]\nFor finite real or complex terms that are eventually nonzero, suppose $L=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}|a_{n+1}/a_n|$ exists, allowing $+\\infty$. If $L<1$, the series converges absolutely; if $L>1$, it diverges. At $L=1$ the test is inconclusive; a missing ratio limit is also no verdict.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n有限实数项或复数项最终非零，且相邻模比极限 $L$ 存在（允许正无穷）时适用。$L<1$ 保证绝对收敛，$L>1$ 保证发散；$L=1$ 无结论，比值极限不存在也不代表发散。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s015",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 590,
      "y": 1260,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[级数根值判别|The root test]]\nFor finite real or complex terms, set $\\rho=\\limsup_{n\\to\\infty}|a_n|^{1/n}$. If $\\rho<1$, the series converges absolutely; if $\\rho>1$, including $+\\infty$, it diverges. At $\\rho=1$ the test is inconclusive. Zero terms and oscillating root magnitudes are allowed.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n有限实数项或复数项，取模的 $n$ 次根上极限 $\\rho$：小于一得绝对收敛，大于一（含正无穷）得发散，等于一无结论。允许零项，也不要求根值有普通极限。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s018",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 1260,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[积分判别余项界|Integral remainder bounds]]\nFor a convergent series satisfying the integral-test conditions from index $N_0$, take $N\\ge N_0$. The remainder after $S_N$, the first $N$ terms, obeys\n$$\\int_{N+1}^{\\infty}f(x)\\,dx\\le S-S_N\\le\\int_N^{\\infty}f(x)\\,dx.$$\nHere $S$ is the finite sum; adding $S_N$ gives an interval containing it.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n先确认级数收敛并从索引 $N_0$ 起满足积分判别条件，取 $N\\ge N_0$。$S_N$ 为前 $N$ 项之和；从 $N+1$ 积分给余项下界，从 $N$ 积分给上界，分别加上 $S_N$ 即夹住有限真值 $S$。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "s019",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1690,
      "y": 1260,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[级数判别法选择|Choosing a series test]]\nStart with defined finite terms and the requested conclusion: convergence, absolute or conditional classification, an exact sum, or an error bound. Match the expression to a theorem and check its hypotheses. Vanishing terms, a ratio/root value of one, or a failed hypothesis alone settles neither convergence nor divergence.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n先核每项有定义且有限，再分清需要收敛判断、绝对或条件分类、精确和，还是误差界。按结构选定理并逐项核前提；通项趋零、比值或根值为一、某条前提不满足，本身都不能判定敛散。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "g-signs",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1640,
      "width": 2180,
      "height": 800,
      "label": "3 · 正负抵消：收敛类型决定怎样估误差与重排",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "s005",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 1740,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[绝对收敛|Absolute convergence]]\nFor finite real or complex terms, $\\sum|a_n|<\\infty$ defines absolute convergence: add the magnitude of each term. This guarantees ordinary convergence, but taking the magnitude after summing is a different operation. Cancellation may still occur.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n对有限实数项或复数项，逐项取模后的级数有有限和，才叫绝对收敛。它保证原级数收敛；先求和再取模是另一件事，绝对收敛仍可发生抵消。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "s007",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 590,
      "y": 1740,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[绝对收敛推出收敛|Absolute convergence implies convergence]]\nFor finite real or complex terms, a finite magnitude sum controls every finite tail of the original partial sums. They are Cauchy: any two sufficiently late totals are close. Completeness then gives a finite sum; merely small individual terms would not suffice.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n有限实数项或复数项的幅度总和有限，就控制原部分和之间的每段有限尾和，使所有足够晚的部分和彼此接近。完备性因此保证有限极限；仅单项趋零不够。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s006",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 1740,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[条件收敛|Conditional convergence]]\nThe original real or complex series has a finite sum, while its magnitude series diverges. Both conclusions are required. Alternating signs alone do not establish this classification; nonnegative real terms cannot be conditionally convergent.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n原实数或复数级数收敛到有限值，同时绝对值级数发散，才叫条件收敛。两项都须证明；符号交错本身不足以分类，非负实数项不可能条件收敛。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "s009",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1690,
      "y": 1740,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[条件收敛重排|Rearranging a conditional real series]]\nFor any prescribed finite real $r$, a conditionally convergent real series admits a bijective rearrangement with sum $r$. Alternating crossings of $r$ have vanishing overshoots, controlling every late partial sum. This does not say every rearrangement changes the sum.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n条件收敛的实数级数可通过每项恰用一次的重排，收敛到任意指定的有限实数 $r$。交替越过目标时，超出量趋零，从而控制所有后期部分和；并非每种重排都会改和。",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "s008",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 2080,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[绝对收敛级数重排|Rearranging an absolute series]]\nFor an absolutely convergent real or complex series, every bijection of the original indices preserves the sum and absolute convergence. Each original index must appear exactly once at a finite position. Every sufficiently late reordered partial sum contains any chosen finite original prefix.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n绝对收敛的实数或复数级数，对原下标作任意双射重排，仍绝对收敛且和不变。每个原下标须在有限位置恰好出现一次；任意选定的原有限前缀，最终会被所有后续新部分和完整包含。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s016",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 590,
      "y": 2080,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[交错级数判别|The alternating series test]]\nFor $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}(-1)^{n-1}b_n$ with finite $b_n\\ge0$, eventual nonincrease and $b_n\\to0$ guarantee convergence. Equal magnitudes and a zero tail are allowed. This test alone does not decide whether convergence is absolute or conditional.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n有限非负幅度 $b_n$ 最终单调不增且趋零，就保证该交错级数收敛，允许相等幅度和零尾部。判别本身尚未区分绝对或条件收敛。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s017",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 2080,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 340,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[交错级数误差界|Alternating remainder bounds]]\nUnder the alternating-test hypotheses, cut within the nonincreasing tail after $N$ terms. If $S$ is the sum and $S_N$ the partial sum, $|S-S_N|\\le b_{N+1}$, and $S$ lies between $S_N,S_{N+1}$. Equality or zero error is possible; this is truncation error, not a rounding bound.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n先核交错判别条件，再在不增尾部截取前 $N$ 项；真值夹在 $S_N,S_{N+1}$ 之间，误差至多下一项幅度。允许等号及零余项；这控制截断误差，不是舍入误差。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "g-power",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2460,
      "width": 2180,
      "height": 780,
      "label": "4 · 幂级数：先定输入范围，再在严格内部运算",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "s020",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 2560,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[幂级数|Power series]]\nFixed real centre $a$ and real coefficients $c_n$ give $\\sum_{n\\ge0}c_n(x-a)^n$. Each fixed real $x$ produces a numerical series; at $x=a$, the sum is always $c_0$.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n幂级数：中心 $a$ 和系数 $c_n$ 固定。每个实数输入得到一条数项级数；中心处始终等于常数项 $c_0$。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "s021",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 590,
      "y": 2560,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[幂级数收敛半径|Radius of convergence]]\nAbout centre $a$, convergence is absolute for $|x-a|<R$ and fails for $|x-a|>R$. $R=0$: centre only; $R=\\infty$: all real inputs. Finite endpoints need separate tests.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n收敛半径是距中心的阈值：内部绝对收敛，外部发散。半径零只在中心收敛；半径无穷覆盖全实轴；有限端点另查。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "s022",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 2560,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[幂级数端点判别|Endpoint tests]]\nFor $0<R<\\infty$, substitute $a-R$ and $a+R$ separately. Convergence may differ, but their magnitude series are identical. Identifying an endpoint sum with a function value needs another argument.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n有限正半径时，左右端点分别代回。普通敛散可能不同，绝对值级数却相同；端点和是否等于目标函数值还须另证。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "s031",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1690,
      "y": 2560,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[幂级数乘法|Power-series multiplication]]\nFor a common centre, multiply in the common absolute interior. Degree $n$ collects $d_n=\\sum_{k=0}^n a_kb_{n-k}$. The new radius is at least the smaller original radius; cancellation can enlarge it.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n幂级数乘法：同中心、共同绝对收敛内部，按总次数卷积系数。新半径至少为原半径较小者；抵消可使它更大。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s029",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 590,
      "y": 2900,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[幂级数逐项求导|Termwise differentiation]]\nFor radius $R>0$, differentiate the powers at real inputs with $|x-a|<R$. A common local tail bound justifies the operation. The radius stays $R$; retest endpoints.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n逐项求导：正半径的严格内部成立，共同局部尾界保证合法。半径不变，但原端点的收敛性不能照搬。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s030",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 2900,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[幂级数逐项积分|Termwise integration]]\nFor $R>0$, integrate over a finite segment strictly inside $|x-a|<R$. Starting at $a$ defines $F$ with $F(a)=0$; antiderivatives are $F+C$ for constant $C$. The radius stays $R$; endpoints need new arguments.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n逐项积分：有限整段须在正半径的严格内部。从中心起积固定 $F(a)=0$；原函数为 $F+C$（$C$ 为常数）。半径不变，端点另证。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "g-taylor",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3280,
      "width": 2180,
      "height": 770,
      "label": "5 · Taylor：匹配导数给候选；余项趋零才给表示",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "taylor-poly",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 3380,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 210,
      "text": "## [[Taylor多项式]]\n共享定义 · 有限次数的导数匹配。\n\n它是候选级数的部分和。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "s023",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 590,
      "y": 3380,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[Taylor级数|Taylor series]]\nIf $f$ has derivatives of every order at the centre $a$, its candidate series is $\\sum_{n\\ge0}f^{(n)}(a)(x-a)^n/n!$. Here $f^{(0)}=f$ and $0!=1$. Finite partial sums are Taylor polynomials; equality with $f$ needs proof.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\nTaylor 级数：中心 $a$ 的各阶导数决定候选系数，$f^{(0)}=f$、$0!=1$。有限部分和是 Taylor 多项式；构造系数并未证明等于原函数。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "s024",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 3380,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[Taylor级数等于函数|When a Taylor series represents its function]]\nFor the Taylor partial sum $P_N$ and remainder $R_N(x)=f(x)-P_N(x)$, equality at a fixed $x$ holds exactly when $R_N(x)\\to0$. Smoothness alone is insufficient; derivative bounds may grow with $N$.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\nTaylor 等式：在固定 $x$ 处，部分和 $P_N(x)$ 趋于 $f(x)$，当且仅当余项 $R_N(x)=f(x)-P_N(x)$ 趋零。光滑本身不足；导数上界可能随阶数增长。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s025",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1690,
      "y": 3380,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[光滑不代表解析|Smooth need not mean analytic]]\nSet $f(0)=0$ and $f(x)=e^{-1/x^2}$ for $x\\ne0$. All derivatives at zero vanish. Its Taylor series about zero converges everywhere to zero, yet $f(x)>0$ off zero.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n光滑不代表解析：零点补零的 $e^{-1/x^2}$ 在零点各阶导数皆零。零级数处处收敛，却不等于任何非零输入处的函数值。",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "taylor-rem",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 3720,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 210,
      "text": "## [[Taylor余项]]\n共享定理 · 高阶导数的区间上界控制有限次数误差。\n\n上界也可能随阶数改变。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "s026",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 590,
      "y": 3720,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[指数函数幂级数|Exponential series]]\n$e^x=\\sum_{n\\ge0}x^n/n!$ for every real $x$; at zero the sum is $1$. Finite Taylor remainders vanish at each fixed input. A fixed truncation still needs its error bound.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n指数展开全实轴成立，零点直接为 $1$。有限 Taylor 余项对每个固定输入趋零；固定截断仍须核对误差界。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s027",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 3720,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[正弦函数幂级数|Sine series]]\nIn radians, $\\sin x=\\sum_{n\\ge0}(-1)^n x^{2n+1}/(2n+1)!$ for every real $x$. All derivatives have magnitude at most $1$, so the finite Taylor remainder tends to zero at each fixed input.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n正弦展开：弧度制、交错奇次幂，分母为对应幂次的阶乘。各阶导数绝对值不超过 $1$，余项对每个固定实输入趋零。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s036",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1690,
      "y": 3720,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[余弦函数幂级数|Cosine series]]\nIn radians, $\\cos x=\\sum_{n\\ge0}(-1)^n x^{2n}/(2n)!$ for every real $x$. It also follows by [[幂级数逐项求导|differentiating the sine series]]: its infinite radius contains every finite input.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n余弦展开：弧度制，从常数 $1$ 开始的交错偶次幂，全实轴成立。也可对正弦级数合法逐项求导；无穷半径的内部包含每个有限输入。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "g-application",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4100,
      "width": 2180,
      "height": 740,
      "label": "6 · 生成可计算的函数：保持定义、展开与误差各自清楚",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "s028",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 4200,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 330,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[对数函数幂级数|Logarithm series]]\n$\\ln(1+x)=\\sum_{n\\ge1}(-1)^{n+1}x^n/n$ for $-1<x\\le1$. Integrate the geometric series inside $|x|<1$; a separate finite remainder proves the endpoint sum $\\ln2$. At $-1$, the series diverges. The function domain $x>-1$ is larger.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n对数展开的等式区间为 $(-1,1]$。内部由几何级数积分得到；右端点用有限余项证明为 $\\ln2$，左端点发散。函数本身的定义域 $x>-1$ 更大。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s032",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 590,
      "y": 4200,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 330,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[幂级数代入|Substitution in power series]]\nFor $R>0$, if $F(u)=\\sum_{n\\ge0}c_nu^n$ for $|u|<R$, substitute $u=g(x)$ wherever $|g(x)|<R$. In $e^u$, $u=-x^2$ works for every real $x$. General $g$ need not leave a power series in $x$.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n幂级数代入：正半径时，通项与输入范围一起替换。指数展开代入 $u=-x^2$ 对全部实数成立；一般复合式未必已是关于 $x$ 的幂级数。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "s035",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 4200,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 330,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[误差函数幂级数|Error-function series]]\nFor every real $x$, $\\operatorname{erf}(x)=\\frac2{\\sqrt\\pi}\\sum_{n\\ge0}\\frac{(-1)^nx^{2n+1}}{n!(2n+1)}$. Finite Taylor remainders bound truncation at all real inputs; the alternating-series shortcut needs a decreasing tail.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n误差函数级数在全实数成立；分母是 $n!(2n+1)$。有限 Taylor 余项界适用于全部实输入；若用交错界，要另查单调尾部。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s034",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1690,
      "y": 4200,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[误差函数|The error function]]\nFor real $x$, $\\operatorname{erf}(x)=\\frac2{\\sqrt\\pi}\\int_0^x e^{-t^2}\\,dt$. It is odd and increasing, with range $(-1,1)$ and limits $\\pm1$ at $\\pm\\infty$. This integral defines it; it is not itself a probability distribution function.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n误差函数先由积分定义。它是递增奇函数，值域 $(-1,1)$；两端极限为 $\\pm1$，有限输入不取到。本身不是概率分布函数。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "gaussian",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1690,
      "y": 4540,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 270,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[高斯积分|The Gaussian integral]]\nBoth one-sided integrals converge. For $e^{-x^2}$, the full-line integral is $\\sqrt\\pi$ and the positive half-line integral is $\\sqrt\\pi/2$. The latter supplies the error function's factor $2/\\sqrt\\pi$.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n两侧分别收敛：全线为 $\\sqrt\\pi$，正半线为 $\\sqrt\\pi/2$。半线值给出误差函数的归一化倍数 $2/\\sqrt\\pi$。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "sequence-limsup",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 440,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 280,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[数列上极限|Sequence limit superior]]\nFor finite real terms $x_n$, the tail ceilings $M_N=\\sup_{n\\ge N}x_n$ are nonincreasing. Their limit is $\\limsup x_n$, allowing $\\pm\\infty$. It records the limiting upper level of whole tails; the original sequence need not converge.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n对有限实数项，先取整个尾部的上确界 $M_N$，再让起点后移。不增的尾部上界的极限就是上极限，允许正负无穷；原数列不必收敛。"
    }
  ],
